Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:47:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] J714s developer image (upstream): linux-aurora up273-7,
 Aura up273-3, Touch ID userspace read-only

linux-aurora 7.3.0.aurora17.up273-7 (aurora-silicon/linux integration/aurora 8679514f plus
betizzel/omarchy-m5 patches/upstream-27.3/0001, 0004, 0005; HEVC on the 27.3 AVE by default) and
m1n1-aurora 1.6.1.aurora24.up273-3 (Aura main d35655304e, with the MTE tag storage #184, plus
0002/0003/0006/0007; 0007 lets the auto-PM storage domain gate itself during the GP PCIe
bring-up), recipes at betizzel/omarchy-m5 222a689. The J714s kernel pins follow the new release
7.3.0-17.up273-7-ARCH.

Two support packages from betizzel/omarchy-m5 installer/recipes (2183b9a):
- aurora-sep 1.17.g8679514f4dff-1 (any): aurora-silicon/linux tools/aurora-sep at 8679514f,
  read-only by default (apple_sep xart_writes=0 provision_keybag=0, no unit enabled).
- libfprint-aurora 1.94.100-1 (aarch64): libfprint 1.94.100 with aurora-sep-userspace
  2ea454e0's aurora driver (sep-bio interface 5).
Both go in the developer profile's support_packages (18 roles), so every image installs them and
the image pin keeps them. finish-inputs accepts an `any` archive (candidate_set still holds
runtime and boot packages to aarch64).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
